WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.462
Unit 2 is the exports and the join.

2
00:00:02.462 --> 00:00:05.663
Every command in the guide's
two export steps is a read.

3
00:00:05.663 --> 00:00:09.405
In AWS, the credential
report lists every IAM user,

4
00:00:09.405 --> 00:00:12.600
its password and its
first two access keys.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.150
It leaves out service-specific credentials
and any key beyond the first two,

6
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.412
so the export also lists access keys
and service-specific credentials.

7
00:00:21.412 --> 00:00:25.862
Then the roles, with their trust
policies, the instance profiles,

8
00:00:25.862 --> 00:00:31.067
the O I D C providers, and the Roles
Anywhere trust anchors, profiles and C R Ls.

9
00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:34.005
List users and list
roles don't return tags,

10
00:00:34.005 --> 00:00:37.363
so the export reads each
user's and role's tags too.

11
00:00:37.363 --> 00:00:41.149
In O C I, against the tenancy's
home region, it reads the users,

12
00:00:41.149 --> 00:00:44.778
each user's credentials, which
come back as identifiers,

13
00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:48.249
never the secret, the dynamic
groups and the policies.

14
00:00:48.249 --> 00:00:53.862
The join is four tags: system I D,
owner one, owner two and sponsor.

15
00:00:53.862 --> 00:00:55.718
Each owner gets its own key,

16
00:00:55.718 --> 00:00:59.599
because an AWS tag value can't
hold a comma or a semicolon.

17
00:00:59.599 --> 00:01:05.350
An identity with no tags or record is an
orphan: disable first, then a person acts.
